module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicTopology.SimplicialObject.Basic
import Mathlib.AlgebraicTopology.SimplexCategory.MorphismProperty
import Sheaf.CategoryTheory.SimplexPresentationFaithful

/-!
# Reconstruction from simplicial operators

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 016B, Lemma `lemma-characterize-simplicial-object`,
parts (2) and (3), with the identities in (1)(a)--(e)
(blueprint: lem-trf-simplicial-operators-reconstruction).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe v u

open CategoryTheory Opposite Simplicial

namespace CategoryTheory

/-- Objects with faces and degeneracies satisfying the simplicial identities determine a
unique simplicial object. A family between two simplicial objects is a morphism exactly
when it commutes with their faces and degeneracies. Equalities of degree objects transport
operators to the prescribed source and target; uniqueness is equality of functors.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 016B, parts (2),(3), using Tag 0168
(blueprint: lem-trf-simplicial-operators-reconstruction).

Proof: (1) In the word presentation `SimplexCategoryGenRel`, evaluate cofaces as `d` and
codegeneracies as `s`, reversing composition. Each of the six defining relations evaluates
to one of the hypotheses (the adjacent mixed identity contributes two relations).
Replacement inside a word preserves evaluation by composition, hence so does the equivalence
relation generated by replacements. Empty words give identities and concatenation reverses
composition, defining a functor out of the opposite presentation category.
(2) The property of simplex maps admitting a lift to the presentation contains identities
and generators and is closed under composition. Apply
`SimplexCategory.morphismProperty_eq_top` (lem-sc-simplex-morphism-property-generators).
The lift is unique by `simplexPresentation_faithful`
(lem-sc-module-cup-godement-simplex-presentation-faithful). Consequently lifts preserve
identities, composition and generators.
(3) Define the functor on `[n]` by `U n` and on a simplex map by evaluation of its unique
lift. The preceding identities give functoriality and the specified operators, using
Mathlib's `SimplicialObject`, `δ` and `σ` (def-weil-pbc-simplicial-object).
(4) For any second such functor, first identify its objects degreewise. Equality of the
maps then contains identities and generators and is closed under composition; the same
morphism-property theorem gives equality on all arrows and thus equality of functors.
(5) For a family commuting with faces and degeneracies, the property of satisfying its
naturality equation contains identities and generators. Substitute the two naturality
equations to check closure under composition, and apply the morphism-property theorem
again. These equations define a natural transformation with the prescribed components.
(6) Conversely, naturality on cofaces and codegeneracies gives precisely the two displayed
commutation equations. Components determine a natural transformation uniquely. -/
theorem simplicialObject_reconstruction {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] :
    (∀ (U : ℕ → D)
      (d : ∀ n : ℕ, Fin (n + 2) → (U (n + 1) ⟶ U n))
      (s : ∀ n : ℕ, Fin (n + 1) → (U n ⟶ U (n + 1))),
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (i j : Fin (n + 2)), i ≤ j →
        d (n + 1) j.succ ≫ d n i = d (n + 1) i.castSucc ≫ d n j) →
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (i : Fin (n + 2)) (j : Fin (n + 1)), i ≤ j.castSucc →
        s (n + 1) j.succ ≫ d (n + 1) i.castSucc = d n i ≫ s n j) →
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (j : Fin (n + 1)), s n j ≫ d n j.castSucc = 𝟙 (U n)) →
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (j : Fin (n + 1)), s n j ≫ d n j.succ = 𝟙 (U n)) →
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (i : Fin (n + 2)) (j : Fin (n + 1)), j.castSucc < i →
        s (n + 1) j.castSucc ≫ d (n + 1) i.succ = d n i ≫ s n j) →
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (i j : Fin (n + 1)), i ≤ j →
        s n j ≫ s (n + 1) i.castSucc = s n i ≫ s (n + 1) j.succ) →
      ∃! X : SimplicialObject D, ∃ h : ∀ n : ℕ, X _⦋n⦌ = U n,
        (∀ (n : ℕ) (i : Fin (n + 2)),
          eqToHom (h (n + 1)).symm ≫ X.δ i ≫ eqToHom (h n) = d n i) ∧
        (∀ (n : ℕ) (i : Fin (n + 1)),
          eqToHom (h n).symm ≫ X.σ i ≫ eqToHom (h (n + 1)) = s n i)) ∧
    (∀ (X Y : SimplicialObject D) (f : ∀ n : ℕ, X _⦋n⦌ ⟶ Y _⦋n⦌),
      (∃ φ : X ⟶ Y, ∀ n : ℕ, φ.app (op (SimplexCategory.mk n)) = f n) ↔
        (∀ (n : ℕ) (i : Fin (n + 2)), X.δ i ≫ f n = f (n + 1) ≫ Y.δ i) ∧
        (∀ (n : ℕ) (i : Fin (n + 1)), X.σ i ≫ f (n + 1) = f n ≫ Y.σ i)) := by
  sorry

end CategoryTheory
